   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to authorizing the commissioner of general services provide\ncompensation to Catholic Guardian Services for certain expenses in connection\nwith holding property for the purposes of providing housing and shelter for\nhomeless, destitute, refugee, delinquent and/or disabled persons in New York\ncity",
    "basePrintNo": "S10339",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S10339-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "General Services, Commissioner of",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10339\n\nSPONSOR: RIVERA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to authorizing the commissioner of general services\nprovide compensation to Catholic Guardian Services for certain expenses\nin connection with holding property for the purposes of providing hous-\ning and shelter for homeless, destitute, refugee, delinquent and/or\ndisabled persons in New York city\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nAuthorizes the Commissioner of the Office of General Services to reim-\nburse Catholic Guardian Services for fair and equitable holding expenses\nassociated with lands transferred to Catholic Home Bureau, which are\nbeing reverted to the State for sale at auction.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the Commissioner of the Office of General Services\nto compensate Catholic Guardian Services for fair and equitable holding\nexpenses, as determined by the Commissioner, associated with property\nlocated at 2322 Valentine Avenue in Bronx County, which is being\nreverted to the State.\n\nSection 2 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is to effectuate the release of the reverter and\nrevesting of title under that certain Letters of Patent, dated August\n24, 2005, recorded on January 20, 2006 in the City Register's Office,\nCounty of Bronx at CRFN 2006000036695. In order to effectuate the\nreverter, the State and Catholic Guardian Services, successor in inter-\nest to Catholic Home Bureau, intend to enter into a letter agreement\nwherein Catholic Guardian Services will provide a deed to the State to\nbe held in escrow. The State will then hold a public auction for the\nproperty under Section 33 of the Public Lands Law.  The deed will be\nreleased from escrow at the closing and the State will convey the prop-\nerty to the successful auction bidder. The State has agreed to reimburse\nCatholic Guardian Services for certain fair and holding expenses to be\ndetermined by the Commissioner of the Office of General Services (OGS),\nwhich will be a percentage of protective costs and expenses previously\npaid by Catholic Guardian Services. The legislation is needed in order\nto give the OGS Commissioner the authority to make such reimbursement\npayment to Catholic Guardian Services in connection with the reverter\nand sale process.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTBD.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nEffective immediately.\n",
